/-!
# Point-orbit witnesses for Sylow overgroups in the Tits group

For each of the 4717 immutable ambient coset words and each of the five
first-parabolic cosets, this table either identifies a word in the second
parabolic or specifies a Sylow normal form and a point of period 5 or 13.
The integer encoding is `n + 2048 * point + 6144 * (prime == 13)`.
The actual verification and its group-theoretic interpretation are separate.

The witnesses were recovered from the preceding attempt's saved calculation;
`source/generate.py` regenerates them from the existing permutation and coset
word tables. Only the Lean kernel checks certify the data.

Source: Parrott (1972), §5, p.683, for the presentation and coset cover;
Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript, printed p.511 (PDF p.528), for the
Sylow-overgroup obstruction used in Proposition 1.3.4.
-/

@[expose] public section

